  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Two-line lay-ups",
  "description": "Two lines at half court or the three-point line, one on each side of the basket. The right-hand line has the balls and shoots, the left-hand line rebounds.\n\nThe first shooter dribbles in with the right hand and makes a lay-up from the right side. The first rebounder runs in, grabs the ball and passes out to the next shooter. Switch lines after every go: the shooter joins the rebound line and the rebounder joins the back of the shooting line.\n\nAfter a few minutes move the balls to the left-hand line and shoot left-handed lay-ups from the left side. Progressions: two balls going at once, or compete for the most lay-ups in a row without a miss.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Right side: right–left steps, take off from the left foot and finish with the right hand."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Aim for the top corner of the square on the backboard."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Rebounder: catch it before it bounces and pass straight to the next shooter."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Keep the speed but stay in control – right steps beat fast steps."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
